{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"consistent lighting for motion tracking consistent lighting for motion tracking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking.md","fileName":"Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Motion Tracking]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Motion Tracking","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"consistent lighting for motion tracking consistent lighting for motion tracking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking.md","fileName":"Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking","heading":"Consistent Lighting for Motion Tracking","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Motion trackers depend on image features remaining recognizable between frames. Flicker, low-light noise, and automatic exposure changes alter pixel patterns and can cause a marker to lose its feature.\n\nFootage should therefore be well lit with stable illumination and, where possible, a fixed aperture. Darkening or flicker can be added during compositing after the clean image has supplied dependable tracking data.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Motion Tracking","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddin